I fixed the last three places where a shell command told the user to type a REPL slash command, and committed it as b7ecda5c with "Fixes #1127" in the title. Build, tests, clippy with -D warnings and fmt all pass.

What changed
• `yoyo lint zz1` now prints Unknown yoyo lint subcommand: zz1 and still exits 2. The shell path goes through the new handle_lint_on with Shell. The REPL's /lint keeps /lint.
• `yoyo skill search` now ends with install with: yoyo skill install gh:<owner>/<repo>. I gave this line a small formatter, skill_search_install_hint, because the search itself needs gh and the network.
• `yoyo skill install <file>` now says yoyo skill install expects a skill directory containing SKILL.md.
• All three use the existing command_form helper, as the earlier #1127 fixes did. I didn't add a second one.

Tests
• Two new tests run the built binary on the shell path (lint zz1 and skill install <file>) and compare whole lines.
• One test checks both REPL and shell output for handle_lint_on.
• The search line is only tested through its formatter, since no test can reach the real search. The REPL and shell paths share the same skill-name value, so the install test exercises the shell wiring.
• Check that the tests can fail: with my two source edits stashed, both binary tests failed; with them back, they pass.
• Two older tests asserted the old Unknown /lint subcommand text on the shell. I updated those assertions to the new wording rather than deleting them.

Probe: I ran all 11 verbs from the ticket on the built binary, in an empty temp dir with a fresh HOME and closed stdin. All exit 2 and none prints a slash form. skill install f also prints the shell form. The full table is in the commit body.

The remaining "/skill" and "/lint" hits in those two files are only doc comments, the code that parses the input, a call that only the REPL's /lint fix makes, and tests. The lint fix refusal on the shell still mentions /lint fix, which is correct: it tells the user to start yoyo first.

Size chore: I added ("src/commands_risk_unhittable.rs", 2036) to the size gate's list of known oversized files, with its real line count. commands_skill.rs grew from 1972 to 1978 lines, still under the 2000 limit.

No docs quoted the old strings, so no docs changed.
